# Maximum Subarray With Equal Products

**Problem:** [Maximum Subarray With Equal Products](https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-subarray-with-equal-products/)

## Approach: Brute Force + GCD + LCM

- Consider every possible starting index `i`.
- Maintain three variables:
  - `g` = GCD of the current subarray.
  - `l` = LCM of the current subarray.
  - `p` = Product of the current subarray.
- Extend the subarray by iterating through `j`.
- Update GCD, LCM and product at every step.
- If `p > g * l`, break because extending the subarray cannot make the product smaller.
- If `p == g * l`, update the maximum length.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int maxLength(vector<int>& nums) {
        int max_len = 0;
        int n = nums.size();

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int g = nums[i];
            int l = nums[i];
            long long p = nums[i];

            for(int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                g = gcd(g, nums[j]);
                l = lcm(l, nums[j]);

                if(p > g * l) break;

                p = p * nums[j];

                if(p == (g * l))
                    max_len = max(max_len, j - i + 1);
            }
        }

        return max_len;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n² × log M), where M is the maximum element.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1), excluding auxiliary space used internally by library functions.
